{"Device-limit enforcement is not atomic: CountDevices and the subsequent insert/update happen in separate statements without any locking, allowing concurrent requests to exceed the configured limit": 0.892482578754425, "tagDeviceUI sets the local cache before calling CreateOrUpdateDevice, so if the write fails due to ErrDeviceLimitReached, the cache key remains and subsequent attempts bypass the limit for the cache TTL": 0.4784276783466339, "TagDevice is called inline with the request context and no timeout, so if the DB stalls, authentication will block and tie up request goroutines under load": 0.9381680488586426}